  "market_context": "Live EUR/USD 1-minute chart during London/NY session overlap; clear micro downtrend with lower highs forming, confirmed by break of structure. Analyst executed multiple short scalps before a stop-loss signaled trend reversal to longs.",
  "key_observation": "Price consistently retraced to the 0.5–0.618 Fibonacci gold zone after each break of structure in the downtrend, enabling high-probability short entries with 1:1.5+ R:R and 2–7 minute holds.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the short-term downtrend by observing lower highs (LH) forming on the 1-minute chart.",
    "Step 2: Wait for a Break of Structure (BOS) — price closing below a prior swing low — to confirm the trend continuation signal.",
    "Step 3: Draw Fibonacci retracement from the most recent swing high (pre-BOS) to the swing low (post-BOS) to define retracement zones.",
    "Step 4: Monitor price returning to the Fibonacci Gold Zone (0.5 to 0.618), preferring entry at 0.618 for optimal risk-to-reward.",
    "Step 5: Enter short position (limit or market) near 0.618, place stop loss above the 1.0 level, and target the previous swing low.",
    "Step 6: Repeat the process for each new BOS while trend holds; exit all shorts when a stop loss is hit, signaling potential trend reversal."
  ],
  "outcome": "First trade closed in 7 minutes; multiple consecutive shorts yielded ~6% profit before one stop-loss hit, resulting in net ~5% gain; then switched to long positions.",
  "lessons": "Scalping works best on 1-minute charts when aligned with micro trend structure; BOS + Fib gold zone provides repeatable entries; a single stop-out is a valid signal to reverse bias.",
